# Does a front NOT aligned with the grid move at the speed it was asked for?
#
# Every other calibration in this suite either uses a front normal to the grid,
# where the answer is exact by construction, or reads the realized speed back
# out of fix ablate.  Neither can see an error that depends on which way the
# surface faces, and the second cannot see one at all: the conversion from a
# speed to a corner point increment and the measurement of what was realized
# share the same projection onto the surface normal, so an error in that
# projection cancels and f_ablate[21] reports the requested speed whatever the
# surface actually did.
#
# So this body is a diamond -- a square turned 45 degrees -- whose four faces
# are all oblique to the grid, and the test measures where the isosurface
# actually is, from the corner point values, outside SPARTA.
#
# FIELD = diamond.smooth   graded corner values, a linear taper across the
#                          interface, which is what the level set relation
#                          needs to know which way the surface faces
# FIELD = diamond.binary   the same body as 0/255 only, which is what
#                          read_isurf produces by default and what a
#                          segmented image gives.  A binary field carries no
#                          direction information on an oblique front: every
#                          crossed edge falls the full 0 to 255 whichever way
#                          the surface is turned.  fix ablate warns about it.
#
# No gas: this is the corner point arithmetic on its own.

variable            RATE index 1.0
variable            FIELD index diamond.smooth
variable            NEVERY index 1
variable            RESP index normal

seed                12345
dimension           2
global              gridcut 0.0 comm/sort yes
boundary            r r p

create_box          0 60 0 60 -0.5 0.5
create_grid         60 60 1
balance_grid        rcb cell

global              nrho 1.0 fnum 1.0
species             air.species N
mixture             air N

variable            rate grid ${RATE}
fix                 ablate ablate all ${NEVERY} 1.0 v_rate mode deposit &
                    units distance response ${RESP}

global              surfs implicit
read_isurf          all 60 60 1 ${FIELD} 127.5 ablate push no

surf_collide        1 diffuse 300.0 1.0
surf_modify         all collide 1

timestep            0.001

dump                D grid all 1500 tmp.oblique.grid id xlo ylo f_ablate[1]
dump_modify         D pad 0

stats               1500
stats_style         step f_ablate f_ablate[21]

run                 1500
